title:: CaosMIDITrackOut
summary:: MIDI output tap for one track: audio and MIDI together.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosMIDI, Classes/CaosTrack, Classes/CaosMIDIOut

description::
Listens to link::Classes/CaosTrack#-onTrigger:: and repeats the current step as a
MIDI note on a link::Classes/CaosMIDIOut::. It does not replace the audio voice;
both outputs sound together.

On melodic tracks the note comes from the current
link::Classes/CaosInstrument#-note::. On percussion tracks the note must be
explicit (for example kick 36, snare 38). The previous note is turned off when
the track triggers again; code::panic:: turns off the pending note.

The tap listens to link::Classes/CaosTrack#-onCommand::, so audio mute/solo does
not stop the MIDI sequence. Playback probability still applies to both.

classmethods::

method:: new
code::
tap = CaosMIDITrackOut(track, midiOut, 36, 100);
::

instancemethods::

method:: track
method:: out
method:: noteNumber
method:: velocity
Read-only tap configuration.

method:: panic
Sends note-off for the last note and clears it. The sequencer does not need to
stop.

method:: free
Calls code::panic:: and releases the track's trigger callback.

